    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a duplicate-telephone rejection to `POST /api/owners` that returns **409 Conflict**, keeping structural impact minimal by adding small, cohesive new units rather than growing existing functions.\n\n**New files (each a single simple function/class, so no surrounding-class complexity to absorb):**\n- `RejectDuplicateOwnerTelephone.java` \u2014 a one-method step that reads the built `@Val Owner` (whose telephone was already normalized by the prior step), scans `OwnerRepository.findAll()`, and throws when any *other* owner shares the same normalized telephone.\n- `DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException.java` \u2014 checked exception (`extends Exception`) so it surfaces in the `throws` clause.\n- `DuplicateOwnerTelephoneExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds 409 with a `ProblemDetail`, mirroring the existing handler pattern.\n- Escalation YAML wiring the exception to its handler.\n\n**One existing file edited (data, not code):** `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted the `rejectDuplicateTelephone` step between `normalizeTelephone` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\nNo existing function bodies were modified, so the only per-function cost incurred is on the new, self-contained functions (WMC_other \u2248 0), and the sole existing-file edit is a YAML pipeline entry.",
